=====================

Fonts are not covered by this license. BIZ UDPGothic (fonts/, @fontsource/biz-udpgothic),
BIZ UDPMincho (fonts/, @fontsource/biz-udpmincho) and Source Sans 3
(@fontsource/source-sans-3) are licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1
(fonts/OFL.txt for BIZ UDPGothic, fonts/OFL-BIZUDPMincho.txt for BIZ UDPMincho;
the @fontsource packages ship their own license files). Built decks embed subsets of these fonts and of the
KaTeX fonts (MIT); those embedded fonts remain under their own licenses.
The default reference voices (tts/voices/bob*.wav, alice*.wav) are synthetic voices
made with Qwen3-TTS (Apache-2.0), Irodori-TTS (MIT) and VoxCPM2 (Apache-2.0); see
tts/voices/README.md. They may be redistributed with this project.
The MP3 encoder of the editor app is not part of this repository's code. The hosted editor
ships the unmodified file dist/index.js of the npm package lame-wasm 0.3.0 (MIT,
https://www.npmjs.com/package/lame-wasm, source https://github.com/dairyisscary/lame-wasm)
as vendor/lame-wasm/index.js, with its LICENSE, package.json and README next to it. That file
contains object code of the LAME MP3 encoder 3.100 as packaged by nixpkgs (LGPL-2.0,
https://lame.sourceforge.io/, source https://sourceforge.net/projects/lame/files/lame/3.100/).
The editor loads it only when a take is encoded, through the module interface init() of
lame-wasm; you may replace vendor/lame-wasm/index.js with another build of lame-wasm or of LAME
that offers the same interface. The single-file editor (editor.html) does not contain it
and saves WAV instead. Its browser TTS window loads onnxruntime-web
(MIT), transformers.js (Apache-2.0) and kokoro-js (Apache-2.0) from jsDelivr, and model weights
from Hugging Face (Irodori-TTS and Semantic-DACVAE: MIT; Kokoro-82M: Apache-2.0); these are
not part of this repository.
